UNIT parse_sig
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 60b55e0a01fec765e82a808a2ede7490c1e3cf116aa0aa28046eb6dcad91682a
SIG export default function parse_sig(s: string): Sig
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime and is driven exactly as js. Declare in the artifact
  type TypeTree = { k: 'text' | 'bytes' | 'bool' | 'none' | 'i64' | 'u64' | 'f64' | 'json' } | { k: 'union'; alts: TypeTree[] }
  | { k: 'tuple'; items: TypeTree[] } | { k: 'list'; item: TypeTree } | { k: 'map'; key: TypeTree; val: TypeTree }
  | { k: 'record'; fields: [string, TypeTree][] };
  type Arg = { name: string; type: TypeTree; rest?: true }; type Sig = { name: string; args: Arg[]; result: TypeTree }.
  An argument carries the property rest only when it is a rest parameter (never rest: false). Property order is
  immaterial. STRICT: the artifact type-checks under strict: true with no any, no non-null assertions (!), no @ts-ignore
  and no @ts-expect-error. A throw (R1, R2, R5–R8) is a thrown Error; the message is not graded. ES module default export;
  imports nothing.
ENVELOPE as the primary; no widening.
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained) a recursive-descent reader with one cursor over the
  string (index access; every accepted character is ASCII): skip WHITESPACE before every token, read IDENT longest first
  by the IDENT pin at the cursor, test literal tokens with startsWith at the cursor. WHITESPACE is the four characters of
  the primary pin only — NOT \s and NOT trim (no-break space, zero width no-break space, line separator, vertical tab and
  form feed are oracle throws). PREFIX (R2): remember the cursor, read the prefix words as IDENT tokens, keep them only
  when each matches and WHITESPACE then an IDENT start follow, else restore the cursor. Unreachable alternatives (R5):
  SAME compares an order-free key of each tree (union alts and record "name=key" fields each sorted, then joined inside
  brackets; tuple, list, map members in order), NOT JSON.stringify of the tree, which is order-sensitive; JSON is a
  recursive predicate over TABLE JSON_SHAPED; COVERS is a recursive predicate that holds when ANY row of TABLE COVERS
  holds (try them all: the LIST, TUPLE, MAP and RECORD rows recurse into COVERS, the union rows recurse both ways); test
  each later alt against every earlier one. Nesting (R8): one depth counter, up on entering a composite, down on its closing bracket. After the result TYPE skip WHITESPACE and require the
  end. A regex match is RegExpExecArray | null and an index read is string | undefined: narrow, never assert.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex IDENT = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/ CITED primary IDENT — applied to the remainder at the cursor
PROVENANCE rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/sir/canon.mjs parseSig + reader. Round 5: re-cut after FINDINGS #74 #78 #79.
